    "summary": "Non-Alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease (NAFLD) and insulin resistance affect over 35% of modern adults, driving chronic fatigue, stubborn visceral belly fat, brain fog, and cardiovascular decay. When chronic sugar and refined starch overload the liver, de novo lipogenesis traps fat inside hepatocytes, blinding insulin receptors. This clinical protocol forces the liver to burn stored hepatic triglycerides and restores cellular insulin sensitivity within 60 to 90 days without lifelong medication.",
