    "summary": "Trembling hands, a cracking voice, dry mouth, and sudden blank mind during presentations or group meetings affect over 75% of humans (Glossophobia). Evolutionarily, speaking before an evaluative crowd mimics being surrounded by hostile predators with nowhere to flee. This neuro-somatic guide overrides the biological freeze response, grounds vocal resonance into the diaphragm, and projects effortless calm.",
