        "title": "Shatter the 'Spotlight Fallacy' (Cognitive Reframe)",
        "description": "Your brain hallucinates that the audience is scrutinizing your every micro-flaw. In reality, audiences are preoccupied with themselves.",
        "code": "# The 3 Internal Truths Before Stepping on Stage:\n1. THE AUDIENCE IS NOT YOUR ENEMY: They actively want you to succeed because watching someone fail makes them feel second-hand embarrassment.\n2. THEY CANNOT SEE YOUR ADRENALINE: Studies prove that while your heart feels like it is pounding out of your chest, 90% of internal agitation is completely invisible to observers.\n3. SHIFT FROM PERFORMANCE TO CONTRIBUTION: Never think: 'How do I look?' Think: 'What is ONE valuable idea I can give them today?'",
