        "code": "# National Cyber Fraud Reporting Action:\n- IN INDIA: Dial 1930 immediately (National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal helpline) or visit cybercrime.gov.in.\n  -> State the UTR transaction number, your bank name, the fraudulent recipient bank/UPI ID, and exact timestamp.\n  -> The 1930 portal automatically fires API lien-freeze instructions to the receiving bank's nodal officer, locking the money in the mule account before it hits an ATM.\n- IN US / INTERNATIONAL: Call 1-800-CALL-FBI (IC3.gov) or file an immediate wire recall request through your bank's SWIFT / Fedwire fraud desk.",
