        "code": "# Formal Bank Claim Letter Draft:\n'To: The Branch Manager / Nodal Grievance Officer, [Bank Name]\nSubject: Notification of Unauthorized Electronic Transaction & Claim under Zero-Liability Mandate\n\nI am writing to report an unauthorized debit of [Amount] on [Date] at [Time], Reference ID: [UTR/TXN ID].\nI have not shared my OTP, PIN, or password with anyone.\nI reported this incident to your customer care within [X] hours (Complaint No: [Number]) and filed Cyber Complaint No: [Acknowledge No].\nUnder Central Bank Consumer Protection Guidelines (Limiting Liability of Customers in Unauthorized Electronic Banking Transactions), my liability is ZERO.\nPlease credit the shadow balance/reversal to my account within 10 working days.'",
        "language": "text",
        "explanation": "Under regulatory guidelines, if a customer notifies the bank within three working days of unauthorized electronic transactions where the deficiency lies elsewhere, the bank must reverse the funds within 10 days.",
