        "description": "If your bank denies zero-liability restitution or delays fund recovery past the statutory 30-day window, escalate through formal regulatory channels: RBI Ombudsman, CPGRAMS, and the Cyber Crime Police Station.",
        "code": "# Formal Regulatory Escalation Workflow (India / International Equivalent):\n1. Draft RBI CMS Grievance (https://cms.rbi.org.in):\n   - Cite RBI Circular: DBR.No.Leg.BC.78/09.07.005/2017-18 (Customer Protection - Limiting Liability).\n   - Attach: Time-stamped bank notification SMS, 1930 Cyber Cell Acknowledgement, and Written Bank Letter.\n2. FIR Section Registration:\n   - Ensure the police register formal FIR under Section 66D IT Act (Cheating by personation using computer resource) and Section 420 IPC / BNS.\n3. Unfreezing Inadvertently Blocked Accounts:\n   - If your clean account was lien-marked by police due to upstream mule fund flow, submit 'Application for Lifting Lien under Sec 451/457 CrPC' before the Judicial Magistrate with audited bank statements.",
