        "stepNumber": 2,
        "title": "Decouple 'Feeling Incompetent' From 'Being Incompetent'",
        "description": "Recognize the Cognitive Distortion: Feeling like an imposter is simply a biological byproduct of operating at the edge of your growth zone. If you feel 100% comfortable, you are stagnating. Adopt the 'Scientist Mindset': you are an investigator running experiments, not a flawless actor performing on stage.",
        "code": "Self-Correction Reframing:\nOld Thought: 'I don't know how to architect this system. Everyone else knows more than me. I am a fraud.'\nReframe: 'This is a novel problem. Nobody knows the exact solution yet. My job is not to know everything instantly, but to research, test, and find the answer.'",
        "language": "markdown",
        "explanation": "True imposters never suffer from imposter syndrome; their Dunning-Kruger cognitive bias convinces them they are flawless.",
