        "title": "Execute the Data-Driven Promotion & Salary Negotiation Meeting",
        "description": "Never ask for a raise based on personal financial need ('my rent went up'). Always anchor the conversation around business ROI, market replacement cost, and forward-looking strategic value.",
        "code": "The Executive Script:\n'Thanks for meeting with me, [Manager]. Over the past 12 months, my scope has expanded significantly. Looking at our results:\n1. Delivered [Project X], which generated/saved [$Y amount].\n2. Mentored 2 engineers and stepped up to lead weekly sprints.\n\nBased on my demonstrated impact and current market benchmarks for Senior [Role] ($Xk - $Yk), I would like to align on adjusting my compensation to [$Target] and updating my title to reflect this level of ownership.\n\nHow do we make that happen over this review cycle?'",
        "language": "markdown",
        "explanation": "Ending with an open collaborative question ('How do we make that happen?') places you and your manager on the same problem-solving team rather than in an adversarial confrontation.",
