        "description": "Hard work alone guarantees you will be taken for granted and passed over for promotion. Meritocracy is a myth; executive promotion requires strategic sponsorship, high-visibility cross-functional initiatives, and boardroom currency.",
        "code": "# Executive Sponsorship & High-Visibility Playbook:\n1. Secure an Executive Sponsor (Different from a Manager):\n   - Identify a VP or Senior Director 2 levels above who sits in compensation calibration meetings.\n   - Value Proposition Offer: \"I am optimizing cross-team API latency by 40%. Would love 15 minutes of your strategic perspective on how this aligns with the company's Q3 enterprise roadmap.\"\n2. The 'Done and Quantified' Bi-Weekly Email:\n   - Send a concise 3-bullet bi-weekly email to key stakeholders:\n     • Delivered: [Initiative] resulting in [$X saved / Y% efficiency boost].\n     • In Flight: [Current high-priority roadmap item].\n     • Blockers: [Clear zero-excuse status].\n3. The Promotion Calibration Dossier:\n   - Prepare a 5-page dossier 3 months before review cycles demonstrating that you are already operating at the next level.",
