        "code": "Place the tightly rolled towel on the edge of the stair step and position your foot so the toes rest extended over the towel while the ball of the foot rests on the step.\n\n1. Understand the biomechanics: When your big toe is dorsiflexed (bent upward), the plantar fascia tightens around the metatarsal head like a cable around a drum (the Windlass mechanism). This places maximum tension on the thick fascial fibers, preparing them for tensile remodeling.\n2. Position your affected foot on the step with the towel under all five toes, forcing them into extension.\n3. Keep your heel hanging completely free off the back edge of the step.\n4. Stand tall near a wall or banister for balance support (finger-touch only, do not pull with arms).",
