        "code": "Perform controlled unilateral (single-leg) heel raises with a strict 3-second concentric rise, 2-second isometric top hold, and 3-second eccentric lower.\n\n1. Concentric phase: Over a full 3 count (1-one-thousand, 2-one-thousand, 3-one-thousand), press through the ball of your foot to rise onto your highest tiptoe.\n2. Isometric pause: Hold at the very top for 2 full seconds. Squeeze calf and arch muscles.\n3. Eccentric phase: Over a full 3 count, lower your heel smoothly until it drops below the stair step, feeling a deep, controlled stretch along the arch and Achilles.\n4. Progression Protocol (Rathleff Clinical Trial Schedule):\n   - Weeks 1–2: 3 sets of 12 repetitions (bodyweight; if single-leg is too painful, perform with both legs together).\n   - Weeks 3–4: 4 sets of 10 repetitions (single-leg).\n   - Weeks 5–8: 5 sets of 8 repetitions, wearing a backpack with 5–8 kg of weights.\n   - Weeks 9–12: 5 sets of 8 repetitions, increasing backpack weight to 10–15 kg.",
