        "code": "# Intrinsic Foot Strengthening & Gait Restoration:\n1. The 'Short Foot' Maneuver (Janda Protocol):\n   - Barefoot on hard floor: Keep heel and metatarsal heads firmly anchored.\n   - Actively pull the ball of the foot toward the heel without curling the toes, raising the medial longitudinal arch.\n   - Hold isometric contraction for 8 seconds. Perform 3 sets of 10 reps daily.\n2. Toe Spreading and Great Toe Isolation:\n   - Lift big toe while keeping 4 lesser toes glued to the floor (10 reps).\n   - Lift 4 lesser toes while keeping big toe glued to the floor (10 reps).\n3. Transition to Wide Toe-Box Zero-Drop Footwear:\n   - Discard narrow, elevated-heel footwear that crunches the hallux into valgus, which pinches the medial plantar artery and chokes blood supply to the heel.",
