        "description": "Inspect the 4 EZ Debug LEDs (CPU, DRAM, VGA, BOOT) on your motherboard to identify exactly which stage fails during Power-On Self Test.",
        "code": "1. Unplug power cord from PC power supply (PSU).\n2. Press and hold the front chassis power button for 15 seconds to discharge capacitors.\n3. Locate the round silver CR2032 coin battery on motherboard.\n4. Pop out the battery with a small flat tool and short the two 'CLR_CMOS' pins with a metal screwdriver for 10 seconds.\n5. Reinsert battery, plug in power cord, and power on.",
