        "description": "DRAM failure accounts for 70% of No-POST and BSOD crashes. Clean RAM contacts with an eraser and test one stick at a time.",
        "code": "1. Release the clips on top and bottom of RAM slots.\n2. Pull out all RAM sticks.\n3. Take a clean pencil eraser and gently rub the gold pins on both sides to remove oxidation. Wipe with microfiber cloth.\n4. Insert ONLY ONE stick into Slot 2 (DDR4/DDR5 standard primary slot: DIMM_A2).\n5. Press down firmly until both clips click audibly. Power on PC. If it boots, test stick #2.",
