        "code": "1. Boot into Windows (or Safe Mode if crashing loops).\n2. Open PowerShell as Administrator and run:\n   Get-ChildItem \"C:\\Windows\\Minidump\"\n3. Download free WinDbg from Microsoft Store.\n4. Open WinDbg > File > Open Dump File > select latest .dmp from C:\\Windows\\Minidump.\n5. In command line, click '!analyze -v'.\n6. Look for \"MODULE_NAME\" and \"IMAGE_NAME\" (e.g. nvgwls.sys = Nvidia GPU driver; netwtw08.sys = Intel Wi-Fi driver).\n7. Reinstall or rollback that exact driver.",
