        "description": "If a PC fails to spin fans or shuts down instantly within 1 second of pressing the power button, the power supply or motherboard has triggered an over-current protection (OCP) short circuit. Test PSU rail voltages under simulated load and inspect the CPU LGA socket for bent pins.",
        "code": "# Power Supply Paperclip Bridge & Multimeter Voltage Check:\n1. Disconnect all PSU cables from Motherboard, GPU, and SSDs.\n2. The 24-Pin ATX Paperclip Jump:\n   - Insert paperclip between Pin 16 (Green wire / PS_ON#) and any Pin (Black wire / Ground).\n   - Flip PSU rear rocker switch to 'I'. The PSU internal fan should spin immediately.\n3. Measure ATX Voltage Tolerances with Digital Multimeter (DC Voltage Mode):\n   - Yellow Wires (+12V Rail): Must read between 11.40V and 12.60V (±5% ATX spec).\n   - Red Wires (+5V Rail): Must read between 4.75V and 5.25V.\n   - Orange Wires (+3.3V Rail): Must read between 3.14V and 3.47V.\n   - Grey Wire (PWR_OK / Power Good): Must output stable +5V. If 0V, PSU internal logic has failed.\n4. CPU LGA Socket Bent Pin Inspection:\n   - Use high-power magnifying glass and angled flashlight to inspect Intel LGA 1700 / AMD AM5 socket.\n   - A single bridged pin causes catastrophic VRM shorts and instantaneous shutdown.",
