        "code": "# VRAM Thermal Pad & Cold Plate Calibration:\n1. Measure Thermal Pad Thickness with Digital Calipers:\n   - GDDR6/GDDR6X Memory Pads: Typically 1.0mm or 1.5mm (check manufacturer schematics).\n   - VRM MOSFET Pads: Typically 1.5mm or 2.0mm.\n   - Hardness: Use soft, high-compressibility pads (e.g. Gelid GP-Ultimate 15 W/mK).\n2. The 'Dry-Fit' Thermal Paste Impression Test:\n   - Install new pads on VRAM and apply thermal paste onto GPU core.\n   - Tighten heatsink screws in an X-pattern.\n   - Remove heatsink immediately and inspect core: Paste MUST be squished into an ultra-thin, transparent layer across the entire silicon die. If paste is thick, pads are too tall and lifting cooler!\n3. Memory Defect Diagnostic Test (MATS/MODS for Nvidia):\n   - Boot into Linux USB containing Nvidia MATS tool:\n   ./mats -e 20\n   - Pinpoints the exact defective VRAM memory bank (e.g. Bank A1, Bank B0) failing read/write address lines.",
