        "description": "When hard acceleration draws high peak amps, the smart BMS disconnects the discharge MOSFETs to prevent thermal runaway. A dead display does not mean a dead battery.",
        "code": "1. Turn off the ignition key and trip the main circuit breaker (MCB) located under the seat storage.\n2. Wait 60 seconds.\n3. Plug the official OEM battery charger into the charging port FIRST, then plug into the wall AC outlet.\n4. The incoming charging voltage (e.g. 54.6V or 67.2V) triggers the BMS wakeup gate, resetting the latching low-voltage or over-current protection circuit.\n5. If the charger LED turns red and fans spin, the BMS has reset successfully.\n6. Turn the MCB breaker back on and test display.",
