        "code": "# Active Equalizer Wiring & Thermal Runaway Containment:\n1. Passive BMS vs Active Balancer Retrofit:\n   - Factory passive BMS bleeders only discharge 30-50mA during full charge.\n   - Wire an auxiliary 5A Capacitive Active Balancer to transfer energy continuously from high-voltage cells to low-voltage cells across the entire cycle.\n   - Double check balance wire sequence: B-, B1, B2, ... B16. A single crossed balance wire will instantly vaporize the BMS traces!\n2. Internal Resistance (IR) Cell Triage:\n   - Measure each cell group IR with an AC milliohm meter (1kHz test signal, e.g. YR1035+).\n   - Normal cell IR: 15-25 mΩ (for 18650) or < 2 mΩ (for prismatic LFP).\n   - If any single cell group shows IR > 2x the pack average, it must be removed. It will act as a localized heater under 30A acceleration draw.\n3. Thermal Runaway Extinguishment:\n   - Keep a bucket of dry vermiculite or Class-D Lith-Ex extinguisher in the EV garage. Standard water/ABC extinguishers cannot stop lithium battery thermal propagation.",
