        "title": "Defective Return Notice (Sec 139(9)) & Income Tax Scrutiny Defense",
        "description": "Filing an ITR with mismatched TDS credits or unverified foreign assets triggers an automated 'Defective Return' notice under Section 139(9) or a discrepancy notice under Section 143(1)(a). You have exactly 15 days to rectify defects before your return is treated as invalid.",
        "code": "# Tax Notice Response & Rectification Workflow:\n1. Access Pending Actions on E-Filing Portal:\n   - Login to https://eportal.incometax.gov.in > Pending Actions > e-Proceedings.\n   - View Notice: Download communication PDF containing the specific mismatch error code (e.g. Error code 83: Gross total income mismatch with 26AS).\n2. Rectify Defect Under Section 139(9):\n   - Select 'Submit Response to Notice u/s 139(9)'.\n   - If error is valid: Upload corrected JSON schema using offline utility with corrected tax credits.\n   - If error is disputed: Select 'Disagree with defect' and provide documentary evidence (e.g. revised Form 16 or employer correction challan).\n3. E-Verification Deadline:\n   - Always verify within 30 days of filing. Failure to e-verify renders your ITR legally void, incurring late filing fee up to ₹5,000 under Section 234F.",
        "language": "text",
        "explanation": "Automated CPC Bengaluru processing compares your return against AIS and banking CTRs using AI algorithms. Failing to respond to Section 139(9) within 15 days treats your return as never filed, triggering interest under 234A and penalty proceedings.",
