        "description": "Fix 'E: Could not get lock /var/lib/dpkg/lock-frontend - open (11: Resource temporarily unavailable)' without corrupting package lists.",
        "code": "# 1. Identify which rogue process is holding the lock:\nsudo lsof /var/lib/dpkg/lock-frontend\nsudo fuser -vki /var/lib/dpkg/lock-frontend\n\n# 2. If unattended-upgrades or apt is hung, kill the exact PID:\nsudo kill -9 <PID>\n\n# 3. Remove stale lock files ONLY if no apt process is running:\nsudo rm /var/lib/apt/lists/lock\nsudo rm /var/cache/apt/archives/lock\nsudo rm /var/lib/dpkg/lock*\n\n# 4. Reconfigure interrupted package installations and clean database:\nsudo dpkg --configure -a\nsudo apt clean\nsudo apt update --fix-missing\nsudo apt install -f",
