        "description": "When Windows Update deletes the Linux EFI pointer or shifts partition numbers, you get dumped into the minimal grub rescue shell.",
        "code": "# At the grub rescue> prompt:\nls\n# Output shows partitions: (hd0,gpt1), (hd0,gpt2), (hd0,gpt3)...\n\n# Inspect each partition until you find where /boot/grub resides:\nls (hd0,gpt2)/boot/grub\n# If it lists files, this is your root partition!\n\n# Set root and prefix paths:\nset root=(hd0,gpt2)\nset prefix=(hd0,gpt2)/boot/grub\ninsmod normal\nnormal\n\n# System boots back into Linux! Now permanently reinstall GRUB:\nsudo grub-install /dev/nvme0n1  # (or /dev/sda)\nsudo update-grub",
