        "code": "# Live USB Emergency Chroot & Snapshot Rollback:\n1. Boot from Ubuntu / Arch Live USB and identify root partition:\n   sudo fdisk -l\n   # Assume /dev/nvme0n1p2 is root, /dev/nvme0n1p1 is EFI partition\n2. Mount Target Filesystem and Bind Kernel Virtual Interfaces:\n   sudo mount /dev/nvme0n1p2 /mnt\n   sudo mount /dev/nvme0n1p1 /mnt/boot/efi\n   for i in /dev /dev/pts /proc /sys /run; do sudo mount -B $i /mnt$i; done\n3. Enter Chroot (Change Root) Environment:\n   sudo chroot /mnt /bin/bash\n   # Now executing as true root on the broken system!\n4. Fix Kernel / Driver Issues inside Chroot:\n   apt update && apt --fix-broken install\n   dpkg-reconfigure linux-image-generic\n   update-initramfs -u -k all\n   update-grub\n5. Btrfs Snapshot Instant Rollback (Alternative):\n   timeshift --restore --snapshot '2026-11-19_22-00-00' --target /dev/nvme0n1p2",
